# Ås station has data all the way back to 1874, so data from 1925 was available. To be able to put them on top of each other we used day of the year on the x-axis.
The mean for 2025 was 7.87 degrees versus 5,28 in 1925. The difference is largest in the autumn and early winter, where 1925 had several very cold periods (down to −20.7 °C). The summers were are quite similar. Years can vary a lot, its not smart to draw any conclusions from just there to years alone. A better comparison would be to use averages over a few years or decades

